# scripts/secret-scan.allow: deliberate fixtures that scripts/secret-scan.sh would report.
# One entry per line, four fields separated by " | ":
#   path glob | kind or * | ERE matched against the found text | reason (required)
# Keep entries narrow: one file (or one fixture directory) and the exact value where possible.

srv/hostcare/testdata/*/dpkg-status.txt | email | .* | verbatim dpkg status of a stock Ubuntu image: public Maintainer/Original-Maintainer fields of distribution packages
srv/hostcare/testdata/*/dpkg-status.txt | public-ip | .* | four-part package version numbers, not addresses
srv/hostcare/testdata/*/sshd-T*.txt | email | @(openssh\.com|libssh\.org)$ | sshd -T output: SSH algorithm names have the form name@domain, they are not addresses
srv/gate/ctl*.go | email | @openssh\.com$ | OpenSSH key type names (sk-ssh-ed25519 at openssh.com) have the form name@domain, they are not addresses
srv/gate/testdata/ctl/*.pub | email | @openssh\.com$ | test certificates made by ssh-keygen: their type names (ssh-ed25519-cert-v01 at openssh.com) have the form name@domain
srv/offsite/key.go | recovery-key | ^tando-key-abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop-qrst-uvwx-yz23-4567-(abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop-qrst-uvwx)$ | the documented text form of a recovery key (the base32 alphabet in order), not a key
srv/offsite/s3_test.go | access-secret | .* | fake S3 credentials for an in-process fake S3 server
test/e2e-alerts.sh | password | =S3CR3Tpw1$ | fake password the test app logs, to prove tando redacts it
* | public-ip | ^1\.1\.1\.1$ | a well-known public resolver: the target of the route lookup that finds a server's source address, and a stock example client address in tests
* | public-ip | ^1\.2\.3\.4$ | the conventional made-up address in help text and test fixtures
test/sec3/net/adopt-fw.sh | public-ip | ^6\.6\.6\.6$ | a spoofed X-Real-IP header value in a firewall test
